      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__mutex_1gaf1857cffa94ba8b3bdf491f1a0096340" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XMutex_Trylock</definition>
        <argsstring>(XMutex *InstancePtr, u8 MutexNumber)</argsstring>
        <name>XMutex_Trylock</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_mutex" kindref="compound">XMutex</ref> *</type>
          <declname>InstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>u8</type>
          <declname>MutexNumber</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Tries to lock a Mutex without blocking. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Locks a particular Mutex lock within a Mutex device. Call returns immediately if the Mutex is already locked (This is Non-Blocking call).</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_mutex" kindref="compound">XMutex</ref> instance to be worked on. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">MutexNumber</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Specific Mutex lock within the device to operate on. Each device may contain multiple Mutex locks. The Mutex number is a zero based number with a range of 0 - (InstancePtr-&gt;Config.NumMutex - 1).</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS if locking was successful.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_DEVICE_BUSY if the Mutex was found to be already locked.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>This is a non-blocking call. The caller gets the lock if it is available. Otherwise, XST_DEVICE_BUSY is returned.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Use XMutex_Lock if you need to block until a lock is obtained. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
